# QA toolchain versions — the single source of truth, for every environment.
#
# A gate's verdict is a property of the BINARY that produced it, not just of the
# repo. Two shellchecks four minor releases apart reported 141 and 173 issues on
# this same tree. Unpinned, that divergence is silent: each environment is
# confident and they disagree.
#
# Only tools a gate RUNS are pinned here. Asserting a tool nothing invokes is a
# gate on nothing, and pinning ansible-lint standalone would give it its own
# ansible-core in a second venv, beside the one run.bash injects into ansible.
#
# Read by all four consumers, so none of them can drift from the others:
#   scripts/qa-toolchain.bash    asserts what is actually installed, every run
#   playbooks/imports/play-python.yml   installs it on the host (the Go toolchain itself
#                                       comes from the play-golang.yml it imports)
#   .claude/ccy/Dockerfile       bakes it into the CCY image
#   .github/workflows/qa.yml     installs it in CI
#
# KEY=VALUE, no quoting, no expansion: it has to be readable by bash `source`,
# by a Dockerfile RUN, and by a GitHub Actions step without any of them needing
# a YAML or JSON parser first.
#
# BUMPING ONE IS A DELIBERATE ACT. A new version is a new gate: change the value,
# then triage whatever findings the new binary invents, re-run
# playbooks/imports/play-python.yml on the host, and rebuild the CCY image
# (`ccy --rebuild`) or every container keeps asserting the old value and fails.

RUFF=0.16.8
SEMGREP=1.177.0
SHELLCHECK=0.11.0
GOLANGCI_LINT=2.14.0

# go-qa-ci (github.com/LongTermSupport/go-qa-ci), the Go QA toolchain: the commit that `go install`
# builds go-qa from, and the checkout whose tools.lock pins ast-grep, gremlins, deadcode,
# govulncheck, gitleaks and actionlint. Those six are installed by the same three consumers from
# that tools.lock, so go-qa is the one version to bump; the sha256 of the release archives are
# pinned inside go-qa-ci, not here. src-go/qa/go.mod requires the same commit (the project rules
# build against go-qa-ci's driver), so a bump changes both.
GO_QA_CI=803b122ce526
